1555 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 1556 0 R/Alt(Flowchart. A main column runs from RTL Design through the oval RTL (SystemVerilog), Logic Synthesis, the oval Gate-Level Netlist, Floorplanning, Placement, Clock Tree Synthesis, Routing, and the oval GDSII to Physical Verification and Tapeout. A dashed region labeled LibreLane encloses the column from Logic Synthesis to Physical Verification, and Parasitic Extraction and Static Timing Analysis on the left. To the right of the RTL, a stack holds Lint, RTL Simulation, and CDC Review. To the right of the netlist, a stack holds Static Timing Analysis, Gate-Level Simulation, Power Analysis, Equivalence Checking, and Scan, ATPG. The oval Constraints (SDC) between the stacks feeds Logic Synthesis and the Static Timing Analysis of the netlist. The oval Testbench feeds RTL Simulation, Gate-Level Simulation, and Post-Layout Simulation. After Routing, a branch on the left runs up through Parasitic Extraction, Static Timing Analysis, and Post-Layout Simulation. Static Timing Analysis and Post-Layout Simulation feed back to Floorplanning, Placement, and, through Design Iteration, to the RTL. Physical Verification feeds back to Routing.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 31182 0 R>>
endobj
