15145 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 15146 0 R/Alt(Block diagram. At the top, data_i enters the D input of the storage block mem_q, whose four entries 0 to 3 feed a 4:1 multiplexer that drives data_o. Below it on the left, push_i and the inverted full_o enter an AND gate, whose output push drives the EN input of the register wr_ptr_q and the EN input of the storage. On the right, pop_i and the inverted empty_o enter an AND gate, whose output pop drives the EN input of the register rd_ptr_q. Each pointer register returns its Q output through a +1 block to its D input and has the inputs clk_i and rst_ni. The lower two bits of wr_ptr_q drive the address A of the storage, and the lower two bits of rd_ptr_q drive the select of the multiplexer. At the bottom, the comparator on the left compares wr_ptr_q with rd_ptr_q with its wrap bit inverted and drives full_o, and the comparator on the right compares both pointers and drives empty_o. Both flags also return to the inverted inputs of the AND gates.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 31305 0 R>>
endobj
